---
interface Props {
    enchArmoNo: number,
    enchWeapNo: number
}
const { enchArmoNo, enchWeapNo } = Astro.props;
---


<section class="clip-shape octagone mod-section">
    <h2>Notes</h2>
    <a style="color: hsl(120, 39%, 63%);" href="#mods-compendium">SKIP</a>
    <ul>
        <li>This page currently covers all the <strong>{enchArmoNo}</strong> armor enchantments and <strong>{enchWeapNo}</strong> of the weapon enchantments available in Tuxborn 1.3 [Beta 3]</li>
        <li>Items in this list are not guaranteed to be in 1.2 final version</li>
        <li>Magnitude is <strong>always</strong> rounded half-down</li>
        <li>All numbers below assume Grand Soul usage</li>
        <li>Locations for the enchanted items are missing</li>
        <li><strong>Remaining Weapon enchantments will be covered in a later update</strong></li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="clip-shape octagone mod-section">
    <h2>Navigation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Click on an enchantment to view more details</strong></li>
        <li>Enchantments's magnitudes at different skill levels are estimations; error is limited to ±1 in most casea</li>
        <li>All enchantments feature a custom rating (S-F)</li>
        <li>Enchantment values at different skill levels are close estimations;
            <ul>
                <li>effects that increase an enchantment's strenght (such as perks) do not influence their value</li>
                <li>values displayed reflect those displayed in inventory and are indipendent of Barter proficiency</li>
                <li>Final value of an enchanted item is the sum of the base item's value with the enchantment's net value</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Filtering options are available to use</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="clip-shape octagone mod-section">
    <h2>Enchanting in Tuxborn</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Tuxborn runs Thaumaturgy to overhaul vanilla enchantments; additionally, many other mods introduce their own learnable enchantments</li>
        <li>Not all enchantments introduced by mods integrate well with Thaumaturgy, often resulting in them being significantly more powerful and remunerative</li>
        <li>For means to further improve your Enchanting see the <a target="_blank" href="https://tuxborn.org/wiki/general-content-topics/crafting/">wiki page on crafting</a></li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="clip-shape octagone mod-section">
    <h2>Bugs and Weird Behaviours</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Enchantment values decrease at higher skill levels due to a vanilla bug</li>
        <li>Most non-Thaumaturgy enchantments have no restriction on what kind of apparel they can be applied to</li>
        <li>Fortify Spell Absorption and various other Artificer weapon enchantments are not learnable due to Legacy of the Dragonborn Patches (Official) editing their item</li>
        <li>Many weapon enchantments from mods have infinite charges or will simply not require any (and have minimum coin value as result)</li>
    </ul>
</section>